1
00:00:09,455 --> 00:00:13,918
KOCHIKAME

2
00:00:14,127 --> 00:00:17,004
&lt;i&gt;Ah, summer's here again&lt;/i&gt;

3
00:00:17,213 --> 00:00:19,924
&lt;i&gt;It's come, it's arrived, it's here&lt;/i&gt;

4
00:00:20,133 --> 00:00:23,010
&lt;i&gt;Ah, summer's here again&lt;/i&gt;

5
00:00:23,219 --> 00:00:25,596
&lt;i&gt;It's come, it's arrived, here it is!&lt;/i&gt;

6
00:00:25,805 --> 00:00:28,850
&lt;i&gt;Big waves, small waves, tiny waves and middle-size waves&lt;/i&gt;

7
00:00:29,058 --> 00:00:31,477
&lt;i&gt;Here they come on the southern wind&lt;/i&gt;

8
00:00:31,686 --> 00:00:34,730
&lt;i&gt;Big boobs, small boobs, tiny boobs and middle-size boobs&lt;/i&gt;

9
00:00:34,939 --> 00:00:37,733
&lt;i&gt;At the beach Jiggle, jiggle, jiggle!&lt;/i&gt;

10
00:00:37,942 --> 00:00:40,736
&lt;i&gt;Ah, summer's here again&lt;/i&gt;

11
00:00:40,945 --> 00:00:43,781
&lt;i&gt;It's come, it's arrived, it's here&lt;/i&gt;

12
00:00:43,990 --> 00:00:46,576
&lt;i&gt;Ah, summer's here again&lt;/i&gt;

13
00:00:46,784 --> 00:00:49,245
&lt;i&gt;It's come, it's arrived, it's here already!&lt;/i&gt;

14
00:00:49,454 --> 00:00:52,498
&lt;i&gt;Big waves, small waves, tiny waves and middle-size waves&lt;/i&gt;

15
00:00:52,707 --> 00:00:55,334
&lt;i&gt;Here they come on the southern wind&lt;/i&gt;

16
00:00:55,543 --> 00:00:58,337
&lt;i&gt;Big butts, small butts, tiny butts and middle-size butts&lt;/i&gt;

17
00:00:58,546 --> 00:01:02,842
&lt;i&gt;At the beach Bounce, bounce, bounce!&lt;/i&gt;

18
00:01:05,928 --> 00:01:15,313
&lt;i&gt;Here they come on the southern wind&lt;/i&gt;

19
00:01:17,815 --> 00:01:21,861
&lt;i&gt;Bouncing at the beach Jiggling at the beach&lt;/i&gt;

20
00:01:23,154 --> 00:01:24,280
&lt;i&gt;Want you!&lt;/i&gt;

21
00:01:28,284 --> 00:01:34,123
SUMO ALL THE WAY!

22
00:01:34,332 --> 00:01:36,167
&lt;i&gt;Hakkeyoi! Nokotta!&lt;/i&gt;

23
00:01:36,375 --> 00:01:39,045
That's it! Come on, Takanoyama!

24
00:01:39,253 --> 00:01:41,839
Yes, like that! Harder! Push him out of there!

25
00:01:42,173 --> 00:01:46,969
Great! That's it! Yes! Now use your special left-hand grab...

26
00:01:48,054 --> 00:01:50,806
Yes! He did it!

27
00:01:54,977 --> 00:01:58,481
That was a true display of strength.

28
00:01:58,689 --> 00:02:02,818
Takanoyama is in excellent form this tournament.

29
00:02:04,904 --> 00:02:10,284
I just didn't want to miss the great Takanoyama's bout.

30
00:02:10,660 --> 00:02:16,457
Can you really feel the actual live excitement of sumo on a TV?

31
00:02:17,875 --> 00:02:21,587
Don't tell me you've seen live sumo.

32
00:02:21,879 --> 00:02:26,092
Well, I have seen real sumo wrestlers wearing yukata on the street sometimes.

33
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:28,052
Even I've seen that!

34
00:02:28,511 --> 00:02:32,473
Well, if you like sumo so much, why don't you go see it live?

35
00:02:32,682 --> 00:02:35,977
Tickets to sumo tournaments aren't that easy to come by.

36
00:02:36,185 --> 00:02:38,563
Oh, really? I didn't know that.

37
00:02:39,063 --> 00:02:44,318
And for a box seat at Kokugikan Arena, you really need to know the right people.

38
00:02:45,152 --> 00:02:50,408
It's been my lifelong dream to watch a sumo match from the box seats there.

39
00:02:51,576 --> 00:02:54,328
Your lifelong dream, huh?

40
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:59,458
&lt;i&gt;Say, doesn't the shopping district&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;have some raffle going on now?&lt;/i&gt;

41
00:03:02,587 --> 00:03:03,754
Hey, Ryotsu.

42
00:03:04,672 --> 00:03:08,009
-Where are you going? -On patrol. Just patrol.

43
00:03:10,511 --> 00:03:15,141
Huh? It's not like Ryo-chan to leave soup behind.

44
00:03:15,349 --> 00:03:16,934
Hmm...

45
00:03:17,602 --> 00:03:22,064
Step right up! Come try your luck in Kameari Shopping District's summer raffle!

46
00:03:22,273 --> 00:03:24,400
We have sumo tickets up for grabs.

47
00:03:25,026 --> 00:03:26,944
Box seat tickets for the final day!

48
00:03:27,153 --> 00:03:29,739
They've yet to be won! Yet to be won!

49
00:03:30,197 --> 00:03:32,074
Raffle tickets... Raffle tickets...

50
00:03:35,369 --> 00:03:37,496
So many lost little lambs.

51
00:03:37,705 --> 00:03:39,248
Uh-oh. This is bad...

52
00:03:39,624 --> 00:03:41,751
Ryo-san wants to enter our raffle.

53
00:03:42,126 --> 00:03:44,670
What? Oh rats. Let's wrap things up for today.

54
00:03:44,879 --> 00:03:48,007
You're being unreasonable. What's wrong with Ryo-san?

55
00:03:48,215 --> 00:03:49,467
Haven't you heard?

56
00:03:49,675 --> 00:03:52,011
That guy has unbelievable luck!

57
00:03:52,219 --> 00:03:56,932
&lt;i&gt;Two years ago, he won a trip to Hokkaido.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Last year, a four-day trip to Guam.&lt;/i&gt;

58
00:03:57,141 --> 00:03:59,727
And he even won a bonus computer!

59
00:04:00,144 --> 00:04:02,188
-Hey! -Urgh...

60
00:04:02,396 --> 00:04:05,274
You aren't closing up shop already, are you?

61
00:04:05,483 --> 00:04:06,442
Look.

62
00:04:09,779 --> 00:04:11,739
All right, let's go!

63
00:04:14,450 --> 00:04:16,952
&lt;i&gt;Let's go, golden ball!&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Give me those box seats!&lt;/i&gt;

64
00:04:17,286 --> 00:04:20,081
&lt;i&gt;Don't you dare come out, golden ball!&lt;/i&gt;

65
00:04:22,083 --> 00:04:23,084
Don't come out!

66
00:04:27,630 --> 00:04:31,467
Argh! He won again!

67
00:04:32,635 --> 00:04:33,469
I won!

68
00:04:36,597 --> 00:04:38,974
Huh? You're back already?

69
00:04:39,183 --> 00:04:39,976
Sure am.

70
00:04:40,685 --> 00:04:43,479
He probably just went around the block.

71
00:04:43,688 --> 00:04:48,234
Hmm? Should you really be talking like that?

72
00:04:49,944 --> 00:04:50,986
-What's this? -Huh?

73
00:04:51,445 --> 00:04:53,197
Oops, how clumsy of me.

74
00:04:53,614 --> 00:04:57,535
-Those are my tickets to the sumo match. -What did you say?

75
00:04:58,077 --> 00:05:00,496
W-Where did you get those?

76
00:05:01,914 --> 00:05:04,417
Well, I guess you could say I know some people.

77
00:05:04,709 --> 00:05:08,421
R-Ryotsu. You're... amazing.

78
00:05:08,671 --> 00:05:10,923
Oh, I wouldn't say that.

79
00:05:11,132 --> 00:05:13,801
So, um, what about...

80
00:05:14,010 --> 00:05:15,678
Let me see...

81
00:05:16,095 --> 00:05:19,390
How about it? Who wants a ticket to see sumo?

82
00:05:19,598 --> 00:05:23,769
Sumo is as symbolic of Japan as the cherry blossom or Mt. Fuji.

83
00:05:23,978 --> 00:05:27,273
All true Japanese people have seen it live at least once.

84
00:05:27,481 --> 00:05:28,733
You there, sir!

85
00:05:28,941 --> 00:05:32,278
Have you been feeling a lack of connection to your roots lately?

86
00:05:32,695 --> 00:05:37,533
Besides, these are box seat tickets. For the final day, no less.

87
00:05:37,742 --> 00:05:42,538
Not exactly something you could buy on a regular old wage, now, is it?

88
00:05:44,206 --> 00:05:48,419
Hmm? Well? Does anybody want a ticket? No? Guess no one wants a ticket.

89
00:05:48,627 --> 00:05:51,839
Well then. Nakagawa, Reiko. Won't you come join me?

90
00:05:52,048 --> 00:05:53,257
-Okay... -Okay...

91
00:05:53,466 --> 00:05:55,468
That just leaves one ticket left.

92
00:05:57,053 --> 00:05:59,638
Of course! How could I forget the most important person?

93
00:05:59,847 --> 00:06:01,682
Oh, well...

94
00:06:01,891 --> 00:06:04,477
I have to invite the old man from the ramen shop.

95
00:06:06,145 --> 00:06:08,314
Ryotsu, you're taking it too far.

96
00:06:08,522 --> 00:06:10,608
He's right! You're being mean.

97
00:06:11,108 --> 00:06:13,027
I was joking! Just joking!

98
00:06:13,235 --> 00:06:16,572
How could I not invite our dear chief?

99
00:06:16,781 --> 00:06:18,616
Chief, you're coming too, right?

100
00:06:18,824 --> 00:06:23,579
W-Well, if you're inviting me. How could I refuse?

101
00:06:24,121 --> 00:06:27,750
By the way, Chief. Don't you have some expensive brandy?

102
00:06:27,958 --> 00:06:30,044
That fancy gift you were bragging about.

103
00:06:30,252 --> 00:06:31,712
Yes, but...

104
00:06:31,921 --> 00:06:35,800
I'll bet brandy from a box seat tastes better than anything.

105
00:06:36,967 --> 00:06:39,053
You want me to bring it? Fine.

106
00:06:39,512 --> 00:06:43,057
Great! Then it's settled. Let's all get back to work.

107
00:06:43,974 --> 00:06:46,560
That's one expensive entry fee.

108
00:06:46,977 --> 00:06:48,896
Like I had a choice...

109
00:06:57,696 --> 00:07:00,533
Ooh, I'm getting excited!

110
00:07:00,741 --> 00:07:02,827
There sure are a lot of people here.

111
00:07:03,035 --> 00:07:07,039
Yeah, and look at how big Kokugikan Arena is.

112
00:07:07,456 --> 00:07:10,292
Of course it's big! Sumo is Japan's national sport.

113
00:07:10,501 --> 00:07:12,169
-Oh! -Sorry.

114
00:07:12,795 --> 00:07:16,382
Oh, sorry! Sorry about that.

115
00:07:16,590 --> 00:07:18,634
&lt;i&gt;Wow, she's gorgeous...&lt;/i&gt;

116
00:07:18,926 --> 00:07:23,514
Uh... This is no program! I-I mean no problem!

117
00:07:23,889 --> 00:07:26,267
Oh, thank you!

118
00:07:29,603 --> 00:07:30,855
Bye!

119
00:07:31,355 --> 00:07:33,899
Looks like lots of foreigners come to watch too.

120
00:07:34,441 --> 00:07:38,529
Yeah, sumo's really popular all around the world these days.

121
00:07:39,238 --> 00:07:41,532
Internationally-acclaimed sumo.

122
00:07:41,740 --> 00:07:44,702
And we get to sit like lords in the best seats.

123
00:07:44,910 --> 00:07:48,497
Now, who do we thank for getting this experience?

124
00:07:48,706 --> 00:07:51,292
Say, I heard somebody won box seat tickets

125
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:54,169
at a raffle at the shopping district the other day.

126
00:07:54,378 --> 00:07:55,171
Uh oh...

127
00:07:55,379 --> 00:07:58,799
I heard it was an officer in uniform.

128
00:07:59,008 --> 00:08:00,092
What did you say?

129
00:08:02,511 --> 00:08:04,096
Is there a problem?

130
00:08:04,305 --> 00:08:06,974
Don't like free tickets? Then you can just leave.

131
00:08:07,975 --> 00:08:13,314
N-No... As long as we get to watch sumo, who cares if the tickets were free?

132
00:08:13,522 --> 00:08:16,400
Ryotsu, I really am grateful.

133
00:08:17,610 --> 00:08:18,819
Well then, let's go.

134
00:08:19,320 --> 00:08:21,030
Everyone got your tickets?

135
00:08:21,238 --> 00:08:22,031
-Yes! -Yes!

136
00:08:22,239 --> 00:08:25,242
All right! Follow me so you don't get left behind!

137
00:08:28,162 --> 00:08:30,664
Ah! My ticket!

138
00:08:30,873 --> 00:08:33,542
Wait! Come here! Come here!

139
00:08:34,919 --> 00:08:36,086
You idiot!

140
00:08:38,005 --> 00:08:41,383
The wind here has a great sense of humor, doesn't it?

141
00:08:41,592 --> 00:08:44,011
Now the three of us can watch sumo in peace.

142
00:08:44,219 --> 00:08:47,056
Let's forget about him and go.

143
00:08:47,264 --> 00:08:48,432
Sure...

144
00:08:48,974 --> 00:08:51,727
-Huh? Oh, look! -What?

145
00:08:51,936 --> 00:08:53,229
Yay!

146
00:08:53,979 --> 00:08:56,440
Thank goodness the current's not strong today.

147
00:08:56,649 --> 00:08:58,734
Did you just jump in the Sumida River?

148
00:08:58,943 --> 00:09:02,446
I sure did! You think I'd lose my precious ticket?

149
00:09:03,072 --> 00:09:06,242
&lt;i&gt;Damn it! You're unbelievable.&lt;/i&gt;

150
00:09:06,450 --> 00:09:08,911
"KOKUGIKAN ARENA"

151
00:09:09,119 --> 00:09:11,997
"SUMO"

152
00:09:18,420 --> 00:09:23,175
On the east side... Nishiki!

153
00:09:24,009 --> 00:09:25,469
Nishiki!

154
00:09:28,305 --> 00:09:30,015
They're just about to start.

155
00:09:30,224 --> 00:09:33,227
You really can't beat live. You really can't.

156
00:09:34,228 --> 00:09:35,354
This is your box.

157
00:09:35,562 --> 00:09:37,481
Hmm, looks kind of cramped.

158
00:09:37,690 --> 00:09:41,235
Well, it's close to the ring. So it's perfect!

159
00:09:42,987 --> 00:09:44,488
What's that?

160
00:09:44,697 --> 00:09:46,156
Snacks and sake.

161
00:09:46,365 --> 00:09:49,702
That's considerate of you. Gotta hand it to box seats.

162
00:09:49,910 --> 00:09:51,996
You also get souvenirs to take home.

163
00:09:52,454 --> 00:09:56,291
And we have the chief's brandy too. This is gonna be a great party!

164
00:09:56,500 --> 00:10:00,004
We didn't come here to party. We came here to watch sumo.

165
00:10:01,088 --> 00:10:03,424
Wow! What fancy binoculars.

166
00:10:04,633 --> 00:10:05,884
Spectator essentials.

167
00:10:06,093 --> 00:10:09,305
Very clever, Chief. Let me see for a bit.

168
00:10:09,513 --> 00:10:10,764
Hold on, me first.

169
00:10:11,932 --> 00:10:14,977
Don't you remember who got us here today?

170
00:10:15,352 --> 00:10:19,064
Again with that? Fine, you can have a look.

171
00:10:19,273 --> 00:10:21,150
Thank you...

172
00:10:23,527 --> 00:10:26,989
Don't see any of those back seaters eating the fancy stuff.

173
00:10:27,197 --> 00:10:29,700
Oh, it's that cute blond from earlier!

174
00:10:30,325 --> 00:10:32,745
If you're not gonna watch, give those back.

175
00:10:32,953 --> 00:10:35,039
It's fine. They won't run out of juice.

176
00:10:35,247 --> 00:10:36,999
That's not the issue!

177
00:10:37,207 --> 00:10:39,585
Well, how about we make a toast?

178
00:10:39,793 --> 00:10:41,503
Oh yeah! I almost forgot!

179
00:10:42,046 --> 00:10:42,963
Cheers!

180
00:10:43,172 --> 00:10:46,133
Wait! Aren't we forgetting something?

181
00:10:46,341 --> 00:10:47,384
-Huh? -What?

182
00:10:47,593 --> 00:10:48,552
What is it?

183
00:10:48,761 --> 00:10:51,263
"Thank you, dear Ryotsu, for your generosity."

184
00:10:51,472 --> 00:10:53,891
Don't you think you should toast to that?

185
00:10:54,099 --> 00:10:55,642
Who would toast to that?

186
00:10:56,060 --> 00:10:57,644
Oh? You don't want to toast?

187
00:10:57,853 --> 00:10:59,313
Excuse me, sir?

188
00:10:59,521 --> 00:11:01,565
This guy's gotta go. Can you get his—

189
00:11:01,899 --> 00:11:05,360
All right, all right already! I'll toast to you.

190
00:11:05,569 --> 00:11:08,072
Thank you, dear Ryotsu, for your generosity.

191
00:11:08,655 --> 00:11:10,491
Cheers!

192
00:11:15,454 --> 00:11:20,459
&lt;i&gt;The great champion, Takanoyama, enters the ring from the west.&lt;/i&gt;

193
00:11:20,751 --> 00:11:23,462
Oh, look! It's Takanoyama! It's really him!

194
00:11:24,338 --> 00:11:27,966
Seeing him live makes you appreciate him even more!

195
00:11:28,342 --> 00:11:30,886
I can't wait for the final bout.

196
00:11:31,095 --> 00:11:31,970
Me neither.

197
00:11:32,179 --> 00:11:36,183
Both are unbeaten so far. I wonder what techniques they'll use?

198
00:11:36,392 --> 00:11:37,476
This is so exciting!

199
00:11:37,935 --> 00:11:41,105
So this is intermission lunch, huh?

200
00:11:41,563 --> 00:11:44,233
Maybe you should settle down and watch the match.

201
00:11:44,441 --> 00:11:46,360
Well, I haven't had lunch yet.

202
00:11:47,820 --> 00:11:49,613
Can I have your sushi, Reiko?

203
00:11:49,822 --> 00:11:51,573
Go ahead.

204
00:11:51,782 --> 00:11:52,616
Thanks.

205
00:11:53,492 --> 00:11:55,953
He sure is eating a lot.

206
00:11:56,161 --> 00:11:59,706
Leave him be. At least he's quiet this way.

207
00:11:59,915 --> 00:12:02,918
On the east side...

208
00:12:03,127 --> 00:12:09,800
Mayunoumi.

209
00:12:10,509 --> 00:12:15,681
Mayunoumi could get into the double digits, so he looks pretty focused.

210
00:12:15,889 --> 00:12:19,435
It's not like on TV. You can really feel their raw spirit.

211
00:12:19,810 --> 00:12:21,145
&lt;i&gt;Hakkeyoi! Nokotta!&lt;/i&gt;

212
00:12:21,603 --> 00:12:24,022
Yes! That's it! Push him! Push him!

213
00:12:24,231 --> 00:12:27,317
Hey, Chief. Hey. Hey, Chief.

214
00:12:27,526 --> 00:12:28,944
What is it? Be quiet!

215
00:12:29,153 --> 00:12:31,155
Can I have your yakitori, Chief?

216
00:12:31,655 --> 00:12:34,575
Yeah, whatever. Quit bothering me—

217
00:12:35,617 --> 00:12:37,077
Damn it!

218
00:12:37,536 --> 00:12:39,538
I missed it!

219
00:12:39,913 --> 00:12:42,541
Mayunoumi.

220
00:12:42,749 --> 00:12:44,126
What an amazing technique!

221
00:12:44,334 --> 00:12:45,377
That was brilliant!

222
00:12:45,586 --> 00:12:47,504
I've never seen anything like it!

223
00:12:47,838 --> 00:12:50,924
You moron! I missed the fight because of you!

224
00:12:51,133 --> 00:12:53,302
But you'd have been mad if I didn't ask.

225
00:12:53,510 --> 00:12:56,597
Who cares about that! Seriously, you...

226
00:12:56,805 --> 00:12:58,724
But you get fussy with your food.

227
00:12:58,932 --> 00:13:00,267
What did you say?!

228
00:13:03,687 --> 00:13:06,773
I'm sick of this! I'm going to the bathroom.

229
00:13:07,441 --> 00:13:09,651
I've had it up to here with him!

230
00:13:09,860 --> 00:13:13,155
Hmph, making a fuss over missing one little bout.

231
00:13:13,363 --> 00:13:14,740
Of course he's mad.

232
00:13:14,948 --> 00:13:18,118
He was really looking forward to seeing Mayunoumi's bout.

233
00:13:18,327 --> 00:13:20,996
It'll be on TV when he gets home, right?

234
00:13:21,205 --> 00:13:23,916
Then why even come here in person?

235
00:13:24,333 --> 00:13:26,168
Look here! Who exactly do you—

236
00:13:26,376 --> 00:13:28,086
Ugh, not that again.

237
00:13:28,295 --> 00:13:30,380
You won that raffle during work hours.

238
00:13:32,716 --> 00:13:34,801
The chief's been gone for a while now.

239
00:13:35,010 --> 00:13:37,221
Did he get lost or something?

240
00:13:38,847 --> 00:13:41,975
Guess it's up to me to find him.

241
00:13:48,440 --> 00:13:49,691
Oh, it's you.

242
00:13:50,025 --> 00:13:53,153
Oh, sorry! Are you okay?

243
00:13:54,029 --> 00:13:57,824
-Keep your eyes peeled for pickpockets. -Yes, sir.

244
00:13:58,617 --> 00:14:01,245
I'm very sorry! Are you hurt?

245
00:14:01,745 --> 00:14:03,330
W-W-What?

246
00:14:04,081 --> 00:14:06,124
Yeah, I'm okay. Don't worry.

247
00:14:06,333 --> 00:14:10,087
Is that so? I am really sorry!

248
00:14:25,143 --> 00:14:28,188
Um... Hmm...

249
00:14:29,898 --> 00:14:31,900
"EAST: FIRST-FLOOR BOXES"

250
00:14:32,109 --> 00:14:33,610
"WEST 3"

251
00:14:35,028 --> 00:14:36,280
"FRONT 2"

252
00:14:38,282 --> 00:14:40,450
How strange.

253
00:14:40,659 --> 00:14:44,246
I could have sworn I came this way,

254
00:14:49,251 --> 00:14:51,503
Oh dear...

255
00:14:52,129 --> 00:14:54,923
All the entrances look the same to me.

256
00:14:55,132 --> 00:14:56,550
Are you all right, sir?

257
00:14:57,759 --> 00:15:01,763
Oh, yes. It's just I don't know how to get back to my seat.

258
00:15:01,972 --> 00:15:03,265
Chief!

259
00:15:03,682 --> 00:15:04,725
Over here!

260
00:15:05,058 --> 00:15:07,269
Oh, Ryotsu!

261
00:15:07,477 --> 00:15:08,937
He's with me.

262
00:15:09,146 --> 00:15:09,980
I see.

263
00:15:10,439 --> 00:15:14,735
There have been reports of a pickpocket wandering the arena today. Do be careful.

264
00:15:15,068 --> 00:15:18,447
Ah, thanks. I appreciate your hard work.

265
00:15:20,907 --> 00:15:23,952
That was close. I almost got lost.

266
00:15:24,161 --> 00:15:25,329
Come. Let's go back.

267
00:15:25,537 --> 00:15:26,580
Hey, Ryotsu!

268
00:15:26,913 --> 00:15:31,084
Look, there's a stall! Maybe we should get gifts for those back at the office.

269
00:15:32,336 --> 00:15:35,797
Okay, but make it quick! It's nearly the last bouts of the day.

270
00:15:40,510 --> 00:15:43,430
Hmm... What to buy...

271
00:15:44,181 --> 00:15:46,099
Oh, look. Handprints!

272
00:15:46,308 --> 00:15:49,102
Look how big Takanoyama's is.

273
00:15:49,519 --> 00:15:51,563
Hmm, this ain't bad either.

274
00:15:51,980 --> 00:15:55,817
The girls back at the station would pay a lot for some Wakataka merch.

275
00:15:56,026 --> 00:15:58,904
Oh, this fan is very well made.

276
00:15:59,112 --> 00:16:01,531
A gift for myself couldn't hurt.

277
00:16:01,740 --> 00:16:04,242
Hey, how much for this?

278
00:16:05,577 --> 00:16:07,788
What's wrong, Chief? Is there a problem?

279
00:16:08,246 --> 00:16:09,831
I can't find my wallet.

280
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:12,709
How weird. I'm sure I...

281
00:16:12,918 --> 00:16:14,836
Can't take you anywhere.

282
00:16:15,045 --> 00:16:17,297
You sure you didn't just leave it at home?

283
00:16:17,714 --> 00:16:21,551
Don't be silly. I bought a train ticket to get here.

284
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:24,888
Well, I can lend you some money.

285
00:16:25,097 --> 00:16:26,598
With interest, of course...

286
00:16:26,807 --> 00:16:28,558
Huh? What's this?

287
00:16:28,975 --> 00:16:30,977
Hey, this isn't my wallet!

288
00:16:31,311 --> 00:16:33,980
Ah, that's mine!

289
00:16:34,189 --> 00:16:35,899
That's my wallet!

290
00:16:36,108 --> 00:16:38,235
Hold on...

291
00:16:38,443 --> 00:16:40,237
Huh? A lady's wallet?

292
00:16:40,445 --> 00:16:42,489
Thief! There's a pickpocket over here!

293
00:16:42,948 --> 00:16:45,242
N-No! You've got it all wrong!

294
00:16:45,742 --> 00:16:46,993
Where's the pickpocket?

295
00:16:47,494 --> 00:16:49,579
-Here. He stole my wallet! -Over here!

296
00:16:49,788 --> 00:16:51,081
I said you're wrong!

297
00:16:51,289 --> 00:16:52,249
You there!

298
00:16:52,791 --> 00:16:54,459
Chief! Let's get outta here!

299
00:16:55,961 --> 00:16:57,003
Hold it!

300
00:16:57,504 --> 00:16:59,589
You two, stop!

301
00:16:59,798 --> 00:17:00,632
Stop! Now!

302
00:17:00,841 --> 00:17:03,760
Why do I have to run too?

303
00:17:03,969 --> 00:17:07,139
Ryotsu! What the heck is going on?

304
00:17:07,973 --> 00:17:09,391
I have no idea!

305
00:17:14,187 --> 00:17:16,148
&lt;i&gt;That's it! That's when it happened!&lt;/i&gt;

306
00:17:16,356 --> 00:17:19,276
&lt;i&gt;That witch! Pinning her crimes on someone else.&lt;/i&gt;

307
00:17:19,484 --> 00:17:20,777
&lt;i&gt;Damn it!&lt;/i&gt;

308
00:17:21,653 --> 00:17:23,905
&lt;i&gt;Where is she?&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;She must be here somewhere.&lt;/i&gt;

309
00:17:24,239 --> 00:17:26,408
Ryotsu! Tell me what's going on!

310
00:17:26,616 --> 00:17:27,909
Stop!

311
00:17:28,994 --> 00:17:31,955
&lt;i&gt;At this rate, we'll both be caught.&lt;/i&gt;

312
00:17:32,622 --> 00:17:35,751
Chief, I need a sacrifice in the name of truth and justice!

313
00:17:35,959 --> 00:17:37,919
What? Sacrifice?

314
00:17:38,128 --> 00:17:40,547
Chief, look! A UFO!

315
00:17:40,755 --> 00:17:41,548
Huh? Where?

316
00:17:42,215 --> 00:17:43,925
Sorry, Chief!

317
00:17:44,259 --> 00:17:45,051
Got you!

318
00:17:45,260 --> 00:17:46,052
Stop!

319
00:17:51,141 --> 00:17:54,519
They sure are taking a long time. What could they be doing?

320
00:17:54,728 --> 00:17:57,522
You think they both got lost?

321
00:17:57,731 --> 00:18:00,484
Wouldn't surprise me, given those two.

322
00:18:01,109 --> 00:18:02,986
Should I go and look for them?

323
00:18:03,403 --> 00:18:05,739
No need. They'll come back eventually.

324
00:18:05,947 --> 00:18:08,992
Besides, when else will we get to eat our lunch in peace?

325
00:18:09,451 --> 00:18:10,619
I guess you're right.

326
00:18:12,537 --> 00:18:13,330
Hey!

327
00:18:13,663 --> 00:18:14,831
Look! It's Ryo-chan!

328
00:18:15,207 --> 00:18:17,042
What is he doing?

329
00:18:17,250 --> 00:18:18,627
Get out of my way!

330
00:18:21,046 --> 00:18:21,838
Oh no!

331
00:18:22,214 --> 00:18:23,924
Coming through!

332
00:18:26,718 --> 00:18:28,011
-Let's go! -Yes!

333
00:18:30,555 --> 00:18:33,350
-He's the pickpocket. -I am not! You've got it wrong!

334
00:18:33,558 --> 00:18:35,018
But you are an accomplice.

335
00:18:35,227 --> 00:18:36,394
Like I said, I'm...

336
00:18:36,603 --> 00:18:39,606
Damn it! You guys are being difficult.

337
00:18:39,940 --> 00:18:42,150
&lt;i&gt;Where's that blond hiding?&lt;/i&gt;

338
00:18:46,863 --> 00:18:52,160
&lt;i&gt;I sacrificed the chief,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;so I'd better find her. No matter what!&lt;/i&gt;

339
00:18:53,495 --> 00:18:54,287
There she is!

340
00:18:55,288 --> 00:18:58,041
Oh, sorry! Are you okay, ma'am?

341
00:18:58,250 --> 00:18:59,918
Huh? Yes.

342
00:19:01,545 --> 00:19:03,505
Pickpocket! She's a pickpocket!

343
00:19:03,713 --> 00:19:05,090
Oh my God!

344
00:19:05,549 --> 00:19:07,384
You're under arrest!

345
00:19:08,176 --> 00:19:09,761
Stop!

346
00:19:10,136 --> 00:19:11,304
Ryotsu!

347
00:19:11,513 --> 00:19:13,598
-Help! Help! -Hold it right there!

348
00:19:13,807 --> 00:19:15,308
Ryo-chan, what's going on?

349
00:19:20,981 --> 00:19:22,274
I got you, thief!

350
00:19:22,482 --> 00:19:25,193
Damn it! You won't get away!

351
00:19:25,402 --> 00:19:26,403
Oh, no!

352
00:19:28,864 --> 00:19:30,574
Come here!

353
00:19:33,994 --> 00:19:35,996
Get your dirty hands off me!

354
00:19:36,204 --> 00:19:39,624
Can it! You're under arrest for pickpocketing.

355
00:19:39,833 --> 00:19:40,959
Give up already!

356
00:19:41,167 --> 00:19:42,419
What's this?

357
00:19:42,627 --> 00:19:46,423
You're the pickpocket. Let that young woman go, now!

358
00:19:46,631 --> 00:19:50,760
Let me go! This blond is the pickpocket here!

359
00:19:50,969 --> 00:19:53,221
You really think this beauty is a thief?

360
00:19:53,430 --> 00:19:55,599
Yours is the face of a criminal here.

361
00:19:55,807 --> 00:19:57,142
Don't judge!

362
00:19:57,642 --> 00:19:59,269
That man isn't the thief.

363
00:19:59,477 --> 00:20:01,688
He tried to help me.

364
00:20:02,272 --> 00:20:03,898
She's the thief!

365
00:20:04,107 --> 00:20:05,066
That's right!

366
00:20:05,275 --> 00:20:06,234
But...

367
00:20:06,443 --> 00:20:08,695
Yeah right! Where is your proof?

368
00:20:08,904 --> 00:20:09,946
Damn it!

369
00:20:11,364 --> 00:20:14,242
-Hold it right there. -Let go of me!

370
00:20:16,911 --> 00:20:19,539
Look! That's my coin purse.

371
00:20:23,001 --> 00:20:24,628
Ryotsu!

372
00:20:24,836 --> 00:20:27,672
How dare you leave me like that!

373
00:20:27,881 --> 00:20:33,053
Now, now. We all need to make little sacrifices to see justice be served.

374
00:20:33,261 --> 00:20:37,182
And with how much you ran, that'll go toward your daily steps.

375
00:20:38,808 --> 00:20:39,768
Huh?

376
00:20:40,101 --> 00:20:41,311
Don't tell me...

377
00:20:43,938 --> 00:20:48,485
She really put all these wallets in my jacket.

378
00:20:48,944 --> 00:20:50,945
She played her looks to her advantage.

379
00:20:52,530 --> 00:20:55,241
Ah, that's my wallet!

380
00:20:55,867 --> 00:20:58,203
I can't let my guard down for even a second.

381
00:20:58,703 --> 00:21:00,205
You can say that again.

382
00:21:12,592 --> 00:21:17,639
You just have to make a mess of things wherever you go, don't you?

383
00:21:18,098 --> 00:21:20,725
Hey, what's with the attitude, Chief?

384
00:21:20,934 --> 00:21:24,771
Sure, I may mess things up every now and then,

385
00:21:24,980 --> 00:21:27,899
but at least I don't get my wallet stolen.

386
00:21:28,108 --> 00:21:30,068
You're one to talk.

387
00:21:30,276 --> 00:21:33,321
You never even noticed all those wallets in your pocket.

388
00:21:33,530 --> 00:21:35,365
What did you say?

389
00:21:38,034 --> 00:21:39,119
Oh no!

390
00:21:39,828 --> 00:21:41,037
It's about to finish!

391
00:21:41,246 --> 00:21:42,372
Chief, hurry up.

392
00:21:42,831 --> 00:21:45,583
There's only one match left.

393
00:21:45,792 --> 00:21:47,627
It's the title-deciding bout.

394
00:21:47,961 --> 00:21:50,755
Now that's the one thing I need to see!

395
00:21:50,964 --> 00:21:53,007
Ryotsu, we'll talk later.

396
00:21:54,175 --> 00:21:56,052
Let's go! It's the decider.

397
00:21:56,261 --> 00:21:57,971
We can't miss it!

398
00:21:59,097 --> 00:22:03,977
They've completely forgotten they're only here today because of me!

399
00:22:09,274 --> 00:22:11,192
&lt;i&gt;Nokotta! Nokotta! Nokotta!&lt;/i&gt;

400
00:22:11,568 --> 00:22:13,862
We made it just in time.

401
00:22:14,487 --> 00:22:18,908
It was all worth it just to see this one match.

402
00:22:19,617 --> 00:22:21,411
Come on, get him! Yes, like that!

403
00:22:21,619 --> 00:22:25,081
Huh? What's going on? I can't see anything.

404
00:22:25,290 --> 00:22:26,416
Ryotsu!

405
00:22:26,624 --> 00:22:28,585
Damn it! I can't see anything!

406
00:22:28,793 --> 00:22:32,130
Let go! It's the final bout!

407
00:22:36,885 --> 00:22:39,721
-What happened? -It's all over.

408
00:22:39,929 --> 00:22:44,017
Man, what a great match. We'll never see something like that again.

409
00:22:47,103 --> 00:22:49,939
Such... a waste.

410
00:22:51,983 --> 00:22:54,652
&lt;i&gt;The winning move was a slap down.&lt;/i&gt;

411
00:22:54,861 --> 00:22:58,656
&lt;i&gt;Takanoyama wins the tournament&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;with an unbeaten record.&lt;/i&gt;

412
00:22:59,407 --> 00:23:04,412
Ryotsu... Why do you hate me so?

413
00:23:04,996 --> 00:23:09,167
I bring you along for free, and all you do is whine and complain.

414
00:23:10,376 --> 00:23:11,628
What did you say?

415
00:23:11,836 --> 00:23:13,088
&lt;i&gt;The award ceremony.&lt;/i&gt;

416
00:23:13,296 --> 00:23:15,298
Why you... How dare you!

417
00:23:15,507 --> 00:23:16,925
Say that again!

418
00:23:17,509 --> 00:23:20,178
You're fired! This time it's for real!

419
00:23:20,386 --> 00:23:22,680
Now that's taking it too far, Chief!

420
00:23:22,889 --> 00:23:25,517
Shut up! It's what you deserve!

421
00:23:25,725 --> 00:23:26,518
Excuse me?!

422
00:23:26,726 --> 00:23:28,436
Why you!

423
00:23:28,645 --> 00:23:29,437
Damn it!

424
00:23:29,854 --> 00:23:31,940
Oh, another fight's started over here.

425
00:23:32,148 --> 00:23:33,817
Yeah, get him!

426
00:23:38,571 --> 00:23:39,989
Should we do something?

427
00:23:40,198 --> 00:23:43,326
Not much we can do. Just leave them to get tired.

428
00:23:43,535 --> 00:23:44,494
But...

429
00:23:44,702 --> 00:23:47,330
We should never have come.

430
00:23:50,375 --> 00:23:52,293
I'll fire you right now!

431
00:23:55,672 --> 00:23:57,966
TODAY'S DAMAGE REPORT

432
00:23:58,675 --> 00:24:02,303
ZERO

433
00:24:05,139 --> 00:24:06,850
&lt;i&gt;Red means stop. Green means go.&lt;/i&gt;

434
00:24:07,058 --> 00:24:09,686
&lt;i&gt;And raise your hand&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;as you cross the street.&lt;/i&gt;

435
00:24:09,894 --> 00:24:11,646
&lt;i&gt;That's just common sense?&lt;/i&gt;

436
00:24:11,855 --> 00:24:14,399
&lt;i&gt;Well, do you follow it properly?&lt;/i&gt;

437
00:24:14,607 --> 00:24:17,569
&lt;i&gt;All right!&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;I'll teach you all about road safety.&lt;/i&gt;

438
00:24:17,777 --> 00:24:20,697
NEXT EPISODE ROWDY, RECKLESS TROUBLEMAKERS!

439
00:24:20,905 --> 00:24:23,074
&lt;i&gt;Don't miss it!&lt;/i&gt;

440
00:24:32,959 --> 00:24:37,255
&lt;i&gt;Let's keep smiling always&lt;/i&gt;

441
00:24:37,881 --> 00:24:41,509
&lt;i&gt;Even when things go wrong&lt;/i&gt;

442
00:24:41,718 --> 00:24:45,972
&lt;i&gt;Keep a pretty smile on your face&lt;/i&gt;

443
00:24:46,556 --> 00:24:51,019
&lt;i&gt;And go out as if nothing happened&lt;/i&gt;

444
00:24:51,561 --> 00:24:55,148
&lt;i&gt;Hey, show me your smile&lt;/i&gt;

445
00:24:55,356 --> 00:24:59,277
&lt;i&gt;You did nothing wrong&lt;/i&gt;

446
00:25:00,236 --> 00:25:03,823
&lt;i&gt;Hey, show me your smile&lt;/i&gt;

447
00:25:04,032 --> 00:25:07,410
&lt;i&gt;Just like you did before, yeah&lt;/i&gt;

448
00:25:07,911 --> 00:25:12,081
&lt;i&gt;I want you to smile always&lt;/i&gt;

449
00:25:12,790 --> 00:25:17,253
&lt;i&gt;A woman with a frown isn't pretty&lt;/i&gt;

450
00:25:17,754 --> 00:25:23,301
&lt;i&gt;So you should smile as soon as you can&lt;/i&gt;

451
00:25:24,093 --> 00:25:27,013
&lt;i&gt;It's the grown-up thing to do&lt;/i&gt;

452
00:25:39,275 --> 00:25:44,072
KOCHIKAME SEE YOU NEXT TIME!
